# Adding a client

When the user says **"Add client: <Company Name>, id <client-id>"**:

1. Add one entry to `clients.json` at the repo root, keyed by `<client-id>`:

```json
"<client-id>": { "name": "<Company Name>" }
```

2. Do not touch any other file, and do not edit, reorder or reformat existing
   entries — including `default`. The whole point of the setup is that adding a
   client is a one-line JSON change.
3. Commit and push that single file.
4. Print the finished link for the user:

```
https://gurgaon-realestate-prototype.teamrsdigitalgroup.workers.dev/?c=<client-id>
```

Keep `<client-id>` lowercase and hyphenated (`rawat-street`, not `Rawat Street`),
because it goes in the URL.

## How it works

`clients.json` is imported at build time by `lib/clients.ts`. Every page reads
the `c` query parameter server-side through `resolveBroker` in `lib/broker.ts`,
so the company name is in the first byte of HTML — nav, hero, footer, headings,
`<title>` and meta description all come from the same resolved value and there
is no flash of the previous name.

A missing or unknown `c` falls back to the `default` entry, so the plain link
with no query string keeps working exactly as before.

The live site redeploys from `main`, so a new client is live once the push
builds. `https://<worker>/?c=<client-id>` is the check; `https://<worker>/clients.json`
shows which entries actually made it into the deployed bundle.
